course: dictionary
lesson: 7992
title: Context clues: rector
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «A vicar or rector leads a Church of England parish; priests serve in Catholic, Orthodox and Anglican churches.» The clues are vicar, parish, leads and churches, so rector means a church leader.
explain: Look closely at «the parish rector». A parish is a small area with its own church, and the rector is in charge of it. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the person in charge of the parish" fits the sentence, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Now look at «the Rector of the university». Here rector does not mean a church leader. Clues like university and the capital R show it is the head of the university. Same word, different meaning. Always ask: what do the words around it tell me?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Rector» means a priest in charge of a parish in the Church of England, the Episcopal Church or the Catholic Church.
fact: In some schools, colleges and universities, especially in Scotland, the rector is the head.
fact: The house a rector lives in is called «the rectory».
fact: In RE you learn different names for church leaders: vicar, rector, priest, minister and pastor.
exercise: «The parish rector visited the sick on Sunday.» What does rector mean here? | A king who rules a village | *A priest in charge of a parish | A shop that sells bread | A tall tree in the churchyard
exercise: Which word means the house where a rector lives? | parish | pulpit | *rectory | churchyard
exercise: In some schools and universities, especially in Scotland, what is the rector? | *The head | The caretaker | The dinner lady | A pupil who sits at the front
test: Which words are the best clues that rector means a church leader? | Dinner and playground | Sunny and warm | *Church and parish | Maths and science
test: In «the Rector of the university», what does rector mean? | A priest in a village church | A type of cake | *The head of the university | A bird that sings
exam: Which sentence uses rector to mean a church leader? | «The rectory has a big garden.» | «The Rector of the university gave a speech.» | *«The parish rector led the service on Sunday.»
